  "body": "## What is missing\n\nThe user documentation has no reference for the post-processor format. A user who writes or changes a `.cps` post cannot find out what the post receives or what it must write. The user must read the source to debug a post.\n\nThe facts exist, but only for developers:\n\n- `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` describes how to write a `.cps` post.\n- `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` specifies the record stream and its property table.\n- `site/content/guide/check-and-post/posting.md` and `machines.md` describe the workflow, not the format.\n\n## Why\n\nThe maintainer asked on 2026-11-21 for this reference, so that people can debug their posts on their own. He set the priority to P3.\n\n## What to add\n\nA reference page in the user guide (`site/content/guide/reference/`), written in plain English. It names these items:\n\n- The manifest properties of a post and what each one does.\n- The hooks that the engine calls, in the order of the call, with their arguments.\n- The record stream and its properties (from `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md`).\n- The functions and values that the prelude gives to a post.\n- The refusal messages of the post gate, with the cause and the fix for each.\n- How to run a post by itself and see its output, so that a user can find an error.\n- One small complete example post, with its output.\n\nWrite the page from our own documents and code only. Do not use text from any other product (Clean-Room Protocol). Keep the page in step with the code: a test or a link check must fail when a manifest property in `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` is not in the page.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The page is in the user guide and the site builds with it.\n- Each manifest property and each hook is in the page.\n- A user can find the cause of a post refusal from the page.\n- The page has a pointer from `check-and-post/posting.md`.\n\nPriority note: AGENTS.md reserves `P1`-`P3` for defects. The maintainer named `P3` in his own words, so the label stands.\n",
